							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1096.msg10823#msg10823"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1096.msg10823#msg10823">Re: FoT stealing  guild passwords </a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #19 on:</b> September 05, 2004, 09:16:33 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ok, here goes I guess.&nbsp; What Ssnakess said was pretty much correct.&nbsp; As for my joining FoT channels, ya, it was to antogonize Eelyen.&nbsp; It probably pissed off some other FoT members, but I don&#039;t really care.&nbsp; I like FoT fine, even asked Kinladar for help every now and then.&nbsp; The leadership of Ascent never said anything because I avoided them getting wind of it, it certainly wasn&#039;t supported by Honch or Delheru.&nbsp; Alot of people in the channel during a critical part of a raid is pretty distracting, and rude.&nbsp; But I can appreciate the humor and the laugh you all must of had.&nbsp; I still did it better though, because none of you bastards had the balls to say anything. Remember guys, payback&#039;s a bitch&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm1.gif" alt="cwm1" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
